    "result_text": "Those two remaining references are in the acceptance test itself \u2014 a descriptive comment and the assertion that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are absent from the response, both of which are correct as-is. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single persisted `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The build is green (`AcceptanceTest` passes, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n**Format** \u2014 e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`: region (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`/`UNKNOWN`) + 2-digit fiscal year (`27`) + 8 upper-hex HASH8 (`16E6609E`, the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) used by the region-and-hash identity) + a single Luhn CHK (`1`) computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Collisions append `-<n>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **New `MemberId.java`** \u2014 the single source of truth for the format: `of(region, fyCode, hash8)` assembles it (with Luhn CHK), `regionOf`/`fiscalYearCodeOf` read the REGION and FY segments back out.\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** (renamed from `AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 assembles the memberId from region + fiscal year + HASH8 + CHK; collision de-duplication now applies to the `memberId`.\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 field `customerCode`\u2192`memberId`, column `customer_code`\u2192`member_id`; schemas (h2/hsqldb/mysql `VARCHAR(24)`, postgres `TEXT`) updated.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings/methods; `memberId` auto-maps from the entity; `locality`/`timezone` read region off the memberId; `fiscalYear` now reads the FY segment out of the memberId (so it references the memberId).\n- **`OwnerRegion`** \u2014 `regionOf`/`timezoneOf` parse the memberId prefix (via known-region matching) instead of the old dashed code; added `knownRegions()`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated` / `OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 the audit line and structured event now reference `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns the memberId.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` schemas with a `memberId` schema; updated `locality`/`fiscalYear` descriptions. (The `OwnerDto` is generated from this at build time.)\n- Refreshed javadoc in `OwnerIdentity` and `OwnerMembership`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: I widened the DB column to `VARCHAR(24)` because the unified base id (`UNKNOWN` region + FY + HASH8 + CHK = 18 chars) plus a collision suffix is longer than the old `VARCHAR(20)`.",
